  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nAllowing better reflection of ongoing navigations, regardless of them being \"same-document\" or \"cross-document\"\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nCurrently `navigation.transition` is only set for same-document navigations, despite the `navigate` event firing for either same- or cross- document navigation. This limitation is somewhat arbitrary.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nExpose `navigation.transition` whenever there is an ongoing same-origin navigation (e.g. an uncommitted cross-document navigation), regardless of it being intercepted/same-document/cross-document, as long as its is same-origin.\n",
